- Our AI models would be fine-tuned using methods like LoRA or QLoRA to optimize performance while minimizing the environmental footprint through quantization techniques (INT8, INT4).
- To ensure continuity of processing and facilitate access to information across different agents or services, we would implement a microservices architecture with containerization (Docker) and orchestration (Kubernetes), allowing for seamless handovers and efficient resource utilization.
- Monitoring tools like Prometheus and Grafana would be used to ensure the system meets the high availability requirement and quickly identify any issues that could impact response times.
- For data protection, we adhere to GDPR guidelines, ensuring encryption at rest (AES-256) and in transit (TLS 1.3), with appropriate access controls.

This proposed architecture aims to satisfy as many of the client's requirements as possible while highlighting areas where further assessment or customization may be necessary to fully meet their needs.
